(6049822, 887564, 109478, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by curtpetguy:</b></div><hr/><i> hey ding, great job , I had ya in the top 10 close. what other lighting did you use besides the car headlights? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I used a bare speed light from left to simulate the car front light and another speed light with soft box from right.</td>', 'Originally posted by curtpetguy: hey ding, great job , I had ya in the top 10 close. what other lighting did you use besides the car headlights?   I used a bare speed light from left to simulate the car front light and another speed light with soft box from right.', '2010-06-10 10:17:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(6049971, 886768, 41337, '<td valign="top">Congrats Leo. Curious, why those light modifiers when the end result was a very harsh light/contrast effect?</td>', 'Congrats Leo. Curious, why those light modifiers when the end result was a very harsh light/contrast effect?', '2010-06-10 12:54:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6050017, 886768, 72670, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats Leo. Curious, why those light modifiers when the end result was a very harsh light/contrast effect? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I used the modifiers because I never know what the final result will be in the processing. Although I know before hand the general look of the pic, the final result is sometimes different. So, for me, a harsh result is easier to achieve in Post than soft light.</td>', 'Originally posted by yanko: Congrats Leo. Curious, why those light modifiers when the end result was a very harsh light/contrast effect?   I used the modifiers because I never know what the final result will be in the processing. Although I know before hand the general look of the pic, the final result is sometimes different. So, for me, a harsh result is easier to achieve in Post than soft light.', '2010-06-10 13:35:23.000000', NULL, 0),
